.TH HALT 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
halt \- stop the computer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B halt
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B halt
flushes its output and asks the kernel to halt the system.
Every process ends and its open files are closed, so what was written
reaches the disks; then the CPU stops.
The machine's power stays on, and the screens keep what they show.
Arguments are ignored.
.PP
To turn the machine off, use
.BR poweroff (1);
to start again, use
.BR reboot (1)
or the power button.
.SH EXIT STATUS
On success
.B halt
does not return.
If the kernel refuses, it prints the reason on standard error and
exits with 1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR poweroff (1),
.BR reboot (1),
.BR kill (1)
